    )
Description: Implements LEAP (LUG-encoded ancestral projection), a phylogeny-
    based computational framework designed to impute the transcriptional states 
    of unobserved ancestral internal nodes within a reconstructed cell lineage 
    tree. By combining cell lineage tracing with single-cell RNA sequencing 
    (scRNA-seq), the package leverages a set of lineage-committed upregulated 
    genes (LUGs) to map terminal cell transcriptomes back onto the internal 
    nodes of the developmental phylogeny. This enables lineage-informed, 
    longitudinal analysis of cell state dynamics throughout development. The 
    method facilitates the discovery of subtle fate specializations and hidden 
    developmental states that lack prominent transcriptional differentiation, 
    supporting the construction of lineage-resolved cell atlases in complex 
    organisms.
